Hi Carlos,

   Thank you for your interest on the package. I believe that, what you mean by individual survival you would like the estimated lifespans and their 95% credible intervals, isn’t it?

   You can extract those as follows: say that you call your BaSTA output “out”. Although it is a basta object, it works as a list. The estimated ages are in “out$agesQuant”, which is a 3 x ni matrix, where ni is the number of individuals with unknown times of birth and/or death. The columns are therefore the mean and lower and upper 95% credible intervals of the estimated ages at death.

Best,

  Fernando


